# Adversarial repair acceptance

The repair baseline is `deploy/full-candidate-20261104` at
`b72d9cfe18651908d4816d08125f7cbedbfc39f8`, confirmed by `git ls-remote`.
The independent review dated 2026-10-27 invalidates release conclusions drawn
from the affected checkers. Existing receipts remain historical observations;
they are not acceptance of the repaired candidate.

## Required behavior and proof

1. Sessions reject deleted holders and deleted account state through both
   direct lookup and the HTTP authentication path. Explicit accountless token
   use remains supported and tested separately.
2. Failed sign-ins increment the persisted counter atomically, including first
   insertion, expiry and lock transition. Concurrent attempts against one scope
   must reach the configured threshold through the sign-in route. A negative
   control must reproduce the lost-update failure in the former mechanism.
3. Malformed session and unrelated cookies receive a refusal at the site gate
   without an exception escaping its request callback.
4. The journey comparator preserves literal dates and durations. Regeneration
   records its exact source and capture revisions and any unavailable inputs.
5. Acceptance rejects failed navigation, missing playable media, unsupported
   removal evidence and inventory discrepancies. Prepared false-pass fixtures
   must fail before any aggregate result is used.
6. Presentation checks inspect decoded rendered text and resolved links,
   including numeric entities, adjacent inline elements and all quote styles.
7. Event conditions combine independently; overrides follow verified Ruby set
   precedence; type-changing saves apply the appropriate old or new membership
   per event. Differential cases use the pinned Ruby reference. Confirm the
   predicted persistence bypass with a complete isolated save.
8. The legacy-switch recipe lists every switch, the cases actually exercised
   and the remaining documented differences.

Checker authors do not accept their own release claims. Each replacement
checker needs an external adversarial pass before its totals are quoted.
Whole-port DSL/mod compatibility, all parity categories on every backend,
publication provenance, signed-in migration, cold performance and recovery
remain unverified until their own evidence is recorded.

## Boundaries

The engine stays general purpose. Site-specific gate and acceptance changes
belong to the consuming project. No deployment or public publication is
authorized by this repair record. Preserve unrelated checkout edits. Record
validation failures and missing evidence explicitly; do not substitute an
older result or reduce the measured inventory.

## Fresh-capture launcher prerequisite

Inspection found that browser startup selected processes from earlier runs
by profile path and stopped them when their recorded parent was dead. A dead
parent does not establish ownership by the current run. Before a fresh capture,
replace this sweep with retained-profile diagnostics and a regression proving
that startup does not stop prior sessions or remove their profiles. Normal
closure of the browser created by the current run remains required.

Capture admission must check the entire source status, including untracked
files, before allocating output or starting builds and servers. Comparison
already rejects dirty provenance; discovering it only after a full run wastes
the capture. The coordinator freezes all source-writing lanes before capture.
The admission regression supplies a separate invalid-reference backstop, so
removing the source guard cannot make the test contact a real host.

Fresh evidence is written outside the source checkout, with existing directory
aliases resolved before admission. A single ignored filename cannot prove a
complete output subtree is excluded from Git. All child shards must close
before the parent exits, including when another shard fails. Report-only mode
starts no build, engine, browser or Cucumber work.

## Additional checker findings from independent review

Candidate byte grades require an externally supplied full source commit and
valid, clean, matching checkout records for every required operation kind.
Missing, null, malformed, dirty or consistently wrong source identities must
refuse the grade through both library and CLI. An explicitly requested
development comparison has a separate diagnostic verdict and nonzero exit;
it cannot establish candidate acceptance. Record the checker's own source
hashes independently from the earlier captured runtime identity.

Literal duration wording is preserved in rendered text, tooltips and links.
The former N5 word-shape mask is retired. JSON key ordering must not rewrite
localhost ports in arbitrary string values. Counterexamples changing trial
duration or a literal port must fail the actual grader. An absent result
value receives an explicit invalid-record problem rather than an incidental
formatting exception. Original reference and capture bytes stay unchanged.

Unavailable or unparsed sign-in response bodies retain an unknown application
error state. Only observed parsed evidence may yield an affirmative or
negative application-error finding; available HTTP/header metadata survives
partial observation failures. Failed or incomplete journey evidence leads
the report as an invalid grade, without a passing aggregate headline.
